1
00:00:04,963 --> 00:00:07,549
Do you know a show called
<i>Document Memoreal</i>?

2
00:00:07,632 --> 00:00:09,592
It's that famous
day-in-the-life show, right?

3
00:00:09,676 --> 00:00:12,637
That show called and said
they want to do a feature on me.

4
00:00:12,721 --> 00:00:14,556
Say what?

5
00:00:14,639 --> 00:00:17,726
Good morning.
I'm Torihara from <i>Document Memoreal</i>.

6
00:00:17,809 --> 00:00:19,394
Why those outfits and makeup?

7
00:00:19,477 --> 00:00:20,895
We thought we might be on camera too.

8
00:00:20,979 --> 00:00:22,439
I look forward to working with you all!

9
00:00:22,522 --> 00:00:24,691
-The pleasure is ours!
-Thank you.

10
00:00:24,774 --> 00:00:25,608
<i>Wow.</i>

11
00:00:25,692 --> 00:00:27,068
<i>What a handsome man.</i>

12
00:00:27,152 --> 00:00:29,612
<i>To be honest, he is an idiot,</i>

13
00:00:29,696 --> 00:00:33,366
but he works really hard
to get acting jobs.

14
00:00:33,450 --> 00:00:37,370
Everyone is supporting me,
so I want to get on top.

15
00:00:37,454 --> 00:00:40,290
It's good. But if we inflate his ego more,
we can film something way funnier.

16
00:00:40,373 --> 00:00:42,250
<i>It's better to exaggerate things.</i>

17
00:00:42,751 --> 00:00:45,670
<i>I have already sufficiently</i>
<i>captured your charm.</i>

18
00:00:45,754 --> 00:00:47,547
<i>Look forward to the broadcast.</i>

19
00:01:21,206 --> 00:01:24,125
-Midori, it's starting, hurry!
-Wait for me!

20
00:01:24,709 --> 00:01:26,961
Hey, you're looking so restless.

21
00:01:27,045 --> 00:01:28,922
-Well, of course I would be.
-Right?

22
00:01:29,005 --> 00:01:29,923
Thank you.

23
00:01:30,423 --> 00:01:32,175
-Thanks.
-Thank you.

24
00:01:36,262 --> 00:01:37,597
-There it is.
-It's started!

25
00:01:37,680 --> 00:01:39,140
So cool, Konta!

26
00:01:41,351 --> 00:01:44,270
THE UNEMPLOYED DREAM-CHASER
NO MATTER WHAT, I STILL WANT TO ACT

27
00:01:44,354 --> 00:01:46,356
<i>What's with this subtitle?</i>

28
00:01:49,109 --> 00:01:50,151
Hello.

29
00:01:50,235 --> 00:01:51,486
I'm the actor--

30
00:01:53,905 --> 00:01:56,991
Hello. I'm the actor, Konta… Wait.

31
00:01:58,493 --> 00:01:59,828
I'm the actor…

32
00:02:00,537 --> 00:02:01,663
Konta Hoshino.

33
00:02:01,746 --> 00:02:03,540
<i>Do you know this person?</i>

34
00:02:03,623 --> 00:02:04,499
We're rolling!

35
00:02:04,582 --> 00:02:06,751
<i>Hoshino Konta, 33 years old.</i>

36
00:02:08,920 --> 00:02:11,840
-Run away!
-So you have come, Poseidon.

37
00:02:12,549 --> 00:02:13,675
Everyone, it's okay.

38
00:02:14,384 --> 00:02:17,303
I will protect this hospital.

39
00:02:17,387 --> 00:02:18,346
Cut!

40
00:02:19,097 --> 00:02:20,974
-Hey, run away!
-Yes?

41
00:02:21,057 --> 00:02:23,977
-You're an extra, just run away!
-Oh, sorry.

42
00:02:24,060 --> 00:02:27,313
-But I acted with my soul…
-No, just do what you're told to do.

43
00:02:27,397 --> 00:02:29,023
-I'm sorry.
-Don't do anything extra!

44
00:02:29,107 --> 00:02:30,066
Yes! I'm sorry!

45
00:02:30,150 --> 00:02:31,359
Okay, one more time!

46
00:02:32,235 --> 00:02:35,613
<i>His only roles have been extras</i>
<i>in stage plays and TV shows,</i>

47
00:02:35,697 --> 00:02:38,158
<i>and his talents haven't blossomed.</i>

48
00:02:38,241 --> 00:02:41,119
<i>A self-proclaimed actor.</i>

49
00:02:41,202 --> 00:02:42,412
Self-proclaimed?

50
00:02:42,495 --> 00:02:44,330
They're so mean from the get-go!

51
00:02:47,458 --> 00:02:49,586
This is a really magnificent villa.

52
00:02:49,669 --> 00:02:53,381
Well, it's really nothing!

53
00:02:54,132 --> 00:02:55,800
Not a big deal, okay?

54
00:02:56,551 --> 00:03:01,055
<i>Konta lives in this villa,</i>
<i>which was owned by his late grandmother.</i>

55
00:03:01,973 --> 00:03:04,267
<i>Since he can stay rent-free,</i>

56
00:03:04,350 --> 00:03:07,645
<i>it is a huge help for Konta,</i>
<i>who hasn't made it big yet.</i>

57
00:03:10,440 --> 00:03:12,984
Has the narrator been decided yet?

58
00:03:13,067 --> 00:03:14,569
Oh, not yet.

59
00:03:14,652 --> 00:03:17,614
Then please get Koji Yakusho.

60
00:03:17,697 --> 00:03:20,158
No, I don't think we can…

61
00:03:20,241 --> 00:03:21,993
Just ask him, just in case.

62
00:03:22,076 --> 00:03:25,830
Narration is very important for
a documentary. Get someone good!

63
00:03:26,456 --> 00:03:30,627
<i>Konta, we are sorry</i>
<i>we couldn't meet your request.</i>

64
00:03:30,710 --> 00:03:33,046
<i>All you've got is me, Wakana Matsumoto.</i>

65
00:03:33,129 --> 00:03:34,464
<i>Please forgive us.</i>

66
00:03:35,089 --> 00:03:39,052
Hey, if they edit it like that,
it will make me look bad.

67
00:03:39,135 --> 00:03:40,136
Who goes there?

68
00:03:48,186 --> 00:03:54,484
<i>Konta uses this entire villa</i>
<i>as a space for his personal training.</i>

69
00:04:05,995 --> 00:04:08,873
You bastard! Come on!

70
00:04:08,957 --> 00:04:13,544
<i>He seriously practices</i>
<i>using past masterpieces as a model.</i>

71
00:04:15,421 --> 00:04:16,798
Isn't this too mean?

72
00:04:16,881 --> 00:04:18,299
This is bad.

73
00:04:18,383 --> 00:04:21,427
The editing is just malicious, isn't it?

74
00:04:25,139 --> 00:04:28,351
<i>Konta got tired from playing make-believe.</i>

75
00:04:28,977 --> 00:04:31,646
<i>He fell asleep while doing Zen meditation.</i>

76
00:04:31,729 --> 00:04:32,981
Playing make-believe?

77
00:04:33,064 --> 00:04:35,525
I wasn't sleeping.
That was mental concentration!

78
00:04:36,109 --> 00:04:38,152
I'm being made a fool of!

79
00:04:38,236 --> 00:04:40,530
The sea feels good, right?

80
00:04:40,613 --> 00:04:42,740
-It's nice.
-Pleasant, right?

81
00:04:44,367 --> 00:04:45,535
Wait a second…

82
00:04:46,995 --> 00:04:51,499
For us actors,
our bodies are our greatest asset.

83
00:04:51,582 --> 00:04:55,878
So… I spare nothing…
when it comes to training.

84
00:04:55,962 --> 00:04:58,965
Twenty, forty, fifty… Okay.

85
00:05:01,342 --> 00:05:05,388
<i>He chooses vegetables that he can buy</i>
<i>with the little money he has.</i>

86
00:05:05,471 --> 00:05:06,806
Cut that part.

87
00:05:10,435 --> 00:05:12,061
So good.

88
00:05:12,645 --> 00:05:15,023
How poor do they want to make me look?

89
00:05:17,275 --> 00:05:19,652
I can really taste the sun.

90
00:05:19,736 --> 00:05:22,280
<i>Then, a savior appeared!</i>

91
00:05:22,363 --> 00:05:28,202
Mr. Konta. I was just about
to come over and deliver some fish.

92
00:05:28,286 --> 00:05:32,623
<i>The one who saves</i>
<i>penniless actor Konta from poverty</i>

93
00:05:33,374 --> 00:05:37,795
<i>is the one who manages the villa grounds,</i>
<i>the caretaker Mr. Nishigami.</i>

94
00:05:37,879 --> 00:05:39,714
But, I'm doing an interview.

95
00:05:39,797 --> 00:05:41,632
<i>I want him to manage me too.</i>

96
00:05:41,716 --> 00:05:44,052
-Hey, are you filming me?
-Yes.

97
00:05:44,135 --> 00:05:47,638
Hey, what was that just now?
Did she let her true desires out a bit?

98
00:05:56,981 --> 00:05:58,357
The heck?

99
00:05:59,108 --> 00:06:01,861
Mr. Torihara betrayed me.

100
00:06:02,695 --> 00:06:05,573
He didn't look like
such a bad person, though.

101
00:06:05,656 --> 00:06:07,992
No, this editing speaks volumes.

102
00:06:08,076 --> 00:06:09,827
It's like a smear campaign.

103
00:06:11,913 --> 00:06:15,083
<i>Bringing you delicious milk every day!</i>

104
00:06:15,166 --> 00:06:16,876
CONNECTING HEARTS
HIROKAMI DAIRY

105
00:06:18,461 --> 00:06:23,341
<i>The one who saves</i>
<i>penniless actor Konta from poverty</i>

106
00:06:23,424 --> 00:06:28,012
<i>is the one who manages the villa grounds,</i>
<i>the caretaker Mr. Nishigami.</i>

107
00:06:28,096 --> 00:06:31,140
Why are they bridging the ad break
with this video of Mr. Nishigami?

108
00:06:34,018 --> 00:06:38,523
<i>When night falls,</i>
<i>jobless youths gathered at the villa.</i>

109
00:06:38,606 --> 00:06:40,108
Jobless?

110
00:06:40,733 --> 00:06:44,487
This is <i>acqua pazza</i> made with
the sea bream Mr. Nishigami brought us.

111
00:06:45,071 --> 00:06:46,656
These are ordinary people.

112
00:06:46,739 --> 00:06:48,908
<i>Even though</i>
<i>he hasn't made it big as an actor</i>

113
00:06:48,991 --> 00:06:52,620
<i>and has no work, Konta seems happy.</i>

114
00:06:53,329 --> 00:06:56,457
<i>Happiness comes in</i>
<i>different forms for everyone.</i>

115
00:06:58,584 --> 00:07:00,545
<i>Today we're having a barbecue!</i>

116
00:07:00,628 --> 00:07:02,964
<i>Today's meat is top grade</i>

117
00:07:03,047 --> 00:07:06,801
<i>We are unemployed, living on benefits!</i>

118
00:07:06,884 --> 00:07:09,220
Hey, this is terrible! I wanna die!

119
00:07:09,971 --> 00:07:11,389
<i>Benefits!</i>

120
00:07:11,472 --> 00:07:15,059
<i>And so, these youths</i>
<i>who have given up on working</i>

121
00:07:15,143 --> 00:07:17,979
<i>kept on drinking the night away.</i>

122
00:07:18,646 --> 00:07:20,356
How horrible!

123
00:07:20,940 --> 00:07:21,899
Konta!

124
00:07:21,983 --> 00:07:23,776
I have some tea here.
Make sure to drink it.

125
00:07:23,860 --> 00:07:25,069
Oh, thank you.

126
00:07:25,153 --> 00:07:27,947
Heave-ho!

127
00:07:28,030 --> 00:07:30,366
<i>When he doesn't have acting work,</i>

128
00:07:30,450 --> 00:07:34,829
<i>Konta makes a living</i>
<i>by helping out the local elderly.</i>

129
00:07:35,538 --> 00:07:38,374
Oh, what is this? Did he secretly film me?

130
00:07:39,500 --> 00:07:40,585
Wow, it's good.

131
00:07:40,668 --> 00:07:43,713
-I can't stop.
<i>-Was he hungry?</i>

132
00:07:43,796 --> 00:07:46,591
<i>Unable to resist,</i>
<i>Konta ended up eating weeds.</i>

133
00:07:47,383 --> 00:07:48,342
Konta!

134
00:07:48,426 --> 00:07:49,802
No, you got it wrong.

135
00:07:49,886 --> 00:07:51,971
-It's mugwort!
-Huh?

136
00:07:52,054 --> 00:07:54,891
Wait, Pero!

137
00:07:54,974 --> 00:07:56,517
Pero!

138
00:07:56,601 --> 00:07:58,603
Pero, Wait!

139
00:07:58,686 --> 00:08:00,480
Pero!

140
00:08:02,440 --> 00:08:04,066
Okay, let me hold you.

141
00:08:04,150 --> 00:08:07,653
<i>-Konta is being looked down on by a dog.</i>
-Oh, no!

142
00:08:07,737 --> 00:08:08,821
Looked down on?

143
00:08:08,905 --> 00:08:10,448
Literally or metaphorically?

144
00:08:10,531 --> 00:08:12,283
Both, I think.

145
00:08:12,366 --> 00:08:13,201
Heave-ho.

146
00:08:14,202 --> 00:08:15,453
Heave-ho!

147
00:08:20,291 --> 00:08:24,170
<i>Now, he is literally eating dirt.</i>

148
00:08:24,253 --> 00:08:26,464
Well, that was clever.

149
00:08:27,215 --> 00:08:28,758
That's right.

150
00:08:28,841 --> 00:08:32,428
By the way, Mr. Jin,
give me some work once in a while.

151
00:08:32,512 --> 00:08:35,056
No matter how small the role…
Even a tiny role. I'll do it.

152
00:08:35,139 --> 00:08:38,935
<i>Konta is close friends</i>
<i>with the popular actor Jin Ichijo.</i>

153
00:08:39,644 --> 00:08:41,604
<i>To this older colleague,</i>

154
00:08:41,687 --> 00:08:45,650
<i>he throws away his pride</i>
<i>and desperately begs</i>

155
00:08:46,234 --> 00:08:51,072
<i>for a job, even a tiny part.</i>

156
00:08:51,155 --> 00:08:53,032
I told them to cut this part!

157
00:08:56,410 --> 00:08:58,829
WHY DID YOU DECIDE TO BECOME AN ACTOR?

158
00:08:58,913 --> 00:09:04,418
When I was in the third grade,
I acted in <i>Momotaro </i>for a school play.

159
00:09:04,502 --> 00:09:06,087
-Out of focus.
<i>-At that time…</i>

160
00:09:06,170 --> 00:09:07,672
It's out of focus.

161
00:09:07,755 --> 00:09:10,299
Can you even see me?

162
00:09:10,383 --> 00:09:11,884
You can't see me, right?

163
00:09:11,968 --> 00:09:13,177
It's just the fire!

164
00:09:13,261 --> 00:09:15,846
It's just the fire the whole time!
The fire!

165
00:09:15,930 --> 00:09:17,515
This is a documentary about fire!

166
00:09:17,598 --> 00:09:20,059
<i>-…to me, was a very happy moment.</i>
<i>-Fire!</i>

167
00:09:20,142 --> 00:09:21,102
<i>A fire documentary!</i>

168
00:09:21,185 --> 00:09:23,145
I was born to act.

169
00:09:23,229 --> 00:09:26,232
<i>Out of focus!</i>

170
00:09:26,315 --> 00:09:28,276
<i>I truly believe that.</i>

171
00:09:28,359 --> 00:09:30,444
<i>Hey, where even am I in this shot?</i>

172
00:09:31,696 --> 00:09:33,197
<i>Me? What about me?</i>

173
00:09:33,281 --> 00:09:36,701
Midori also supports me.

174
00:09:37,994 --> 00:09:40,955
Everyone is supporting me,
so I want to get on top…

175
00:09:41,747 --> 00:09:44,125
<i>I was saying something good!</i>

176
00:09:53,426 --> 00:09:54,969
Konta!

177
00:09:55,052 --> 00:09:56,387
Get up!

178
00:09:56,971 --> 00:09:59,515
<i>Stop it! Please stop it!</i>

179
00:10:02,018 --> 00:10:03,603
The heck is this?

180
00:10:03,686 --> 00:10:06,314
This editing is way too mean.

181
00:10:10,860 --> 00:10:12,153
Konta?

182
00:10:22,538 --> 00:10:23,456
It's dangerous.

183
00:10:23,539 --> 00:10:29,587
<i>Out of a misguided sense of purpose,</i>
<i>Konta chose the path of an actor.</i>

184
00:10:30,588 --> 00:10:33,591
<i>Although he currently</i>
<i>has no money or work,</i>

185
00:10:33,674 --> 00:10:36,594
<i>with his characteristic</i>
<i>groundless confidence,</i>

186
00:10:36,677 --> 00:10:38,721
<i>he has come far.</i>

187
00:10:40,765 --> 00:10:44,977
<i>However, Konta's groundless confidence</i>

188
00:10:45,061 --> 00:10:48,606
<i>also gives energy</i>
<i>to the people around him.</i>

189
00:10:49,315 --> 00:10:51,901
Mr. Torihara. I'll make you a drink.

190
00:10:51,984 --> 00:10:54,111
But I'm still on the clock.

191
00:10:54,195 --> 00:10:55,821
It's totally fine.

192
00:10:55,905 --> 00:10:59,075
However, if you drink this,
you'll turn stupid!

193
00:10:59,158 --> 00:11:00,201
What?

194
00:11:00,284 --> 00:11:03,037
Wait, Konta, that's way too much.

195
00:11:03,120 --> 00:11:06,040
Mr. Torihara has been filming me
all day today.

196
00:11:06,123 --> 00:11:09,710
His stomach must be rumbling,
so he needs to eat at least this much.

197
00:11:13,547 --> 00:11:17,218
<i>Giving his all</i>
<i>and doing his best in everything</i>.

198
00:11:17,802 --> 00:11:22,640
<i>Everyone looks up to Konta,</i>
<i>who is always bright and laughing.</i>

199
00:11:22,723 --> 00:11:27,895
If I were born a bit earlier,
maybe I would flirt with you!

200
00:11:27,978 --> 00:11:29,522
Oh, you make me blush.

201
00:11:30,856 --> 00:11:32,566
Konta is…

202
00:11:32,650 --> 00:11:34,110
Konta is…

203
00:11:35,653 --> 00:11:36,821
He is an idiot.

204
00:11:37,405 --> 00:11:39,240
I think everyone knows that.

205
00:11:39,907 --> 00:11:45,037
But, I like that idiotic part of him.

206
00:11:45,746 --> 00:11:47,998
He's a fool who doesn't hurt anyone.

207
00:11:48,082 --> 00:11:51,627
Even his stupid alcohol, the flavor
isn't right unless Konta makes it.

208
00:11:51,710 --> 00:11:55,089
That drink has got to be
made by a fool, or it isn't fun.

209
00:11:55,172 --> 00:11:59,343
Since coming to this villa
and spending time with Konta,

210
00:11:59,427 --> 00:12:01,887
I've witnessed how much of an idiot he is,

211
00:12:02,555 --> 00:12:07,143
but I also see
how hard he works for his dream,

212
00:12:07,226 --> 00:12:09,061
and felt it…

213
00:12:09,854 --> 00:12:11,772
How should I put it…

214
00:12:12,565 --> 00:12:15,484
It's nice. Like…

215
00:12:15,568 --> 00:12:17,695
He's charming.

216
00:12:18,821 --> 00:12:20,406
Oh, my.

217
00:12:20,489 --> 00:12:22,450
This is embarrassing!

218
00:12:23,868 --> 00:12:27,788
After coming to this villa,
I have spent so much time with him.

219
00:12:27,872 --> 00:12:29,498
It's like we're kids again.

220
00:12:30,541 --> 00:12:36,172
Well, my brother is an idiot
and usually loud and annoying.

221
00:12:36,881 --> 00:12:38,048
But…

222
00:12:38,674 --> 00:12:42,595
He is aiming to be an actor
and working so hard,

223
00:12:43,262 --> 00:12:47,975
so as his sister,
I feel I have to support him.

224
00:12:49,226 --> 00:12:52,855
Even if he's a fool,
if he can be a fool for acting,

225
00:12:52,938 --> 00:12:55,107
I guess that would be great.

226
00:12:56,233 --> 00:12:58,861
"I'll buy it because Konta Hoshino
is on the cover."

227
00:12:58,944 --> 00:13:01,405
"I'll watch it
because Konta Hoshino is in it."

228
00:13:01,489 --> 00:13:05,784
I want to create
a Konta Hoshino sensation like that.

229
00:13:07,661 --> 00:13:11,957
<i>The jobless friends who support Konta.</i>

230
00:13:13,751 --> 00:13:17,630
<i>The cool Mr. Nishigami</i>
<i>who watches over him.</i>

231
00:13:19,757 --> 00:13:22,593
<i>Konta's groundless confidence</i>…

232
00:13:22,676 --> 00:13:28,140
<i>Is his driving force to keep chasing</i>
<i>his big dream of being an actor.</i>

233
00:13:29,225 --> 00:13:32,311
<i>Someday, that confidence</i>
<i>might become real,</i>

234
00:13:32,394 --> 00:13:36,857
<i>and the day may come when the Konta</i>
<i>Hoshino boom takes the world by storm.</i>

235
00:13:40,611 --> 00:13:41,695
<i>Until that day</i>…

236
00:13:42,530 --> 00:13:45,032
<i>we want to keep watching over him.</i>

237
00:13:46,492 --> 00:13:47,660
<i>Konta!</i>

238
00:13:48,244 --> 00:13:50,621
<i>Everyone is rooting for you!</i>

239
00:13:58,921 --> 00:13:59,964
So in the end…

240
00:14:00,047 --> 00:14:03,217
It shows that Konta
is a lovable guy, right?

241
00:14:03,300 --> 00:14:04,176
Yeah.

242
00:14:04,260 --> 00:14:07,680
And my brother
didn't even watch it until the end.

243
00:14:07,763 --> 00:14:09,473
He really is an idiot.

244
00:14:10,099 --> 00:14:11,058
Oh, look.

245
00:14:11,141 --> 00:14:13,727
-What?
-The hashtag #WeedEatingMan is trending!

246
00:14:13,811 --> 00:14:16,146
-What?
-The part where he was eating mugwort?

247
00:14:16,230 --> 00:14:17,356
-Seriously?
-Look!

248
00:14:17,439 --> 00:14:19,066
-Amazing!
-It's true!

249
00:14:19,149 --> 00:14:20,776
Wow!

250
00:14:20,860 --> 00:14:21,735
Right?

251
00:14:21,819 --> 00:14:23,279
Everyone's posting.

252
00:14:23,362 --> 00:14:24,530
-Amazing.
-How stupid.

253
00:14:25,114 --> 00:14:26,240
-Amazing!
-This part…

254
00:14:26,323 --> 00:14:27,408
Oh, wow.

255
00:14:27,491 --> 00:14:28,826
-It's going viral.
-Wow.

256
00:14:28,909 --> 00:14:31,120
-How stupid.
-What a funny pic.

257
00:14:31,203 --> 00:14:32,997
-It's going viral.
-Wow!

258
00:15:02,610 --> 00:15:03,694
Konta.

259
00:15:03,777 --> 00:15:06,113
Dinner is ready. Aren't you going to eat?

260
00:15:24,173 --> 00:15:25,090
Mr. Konta.

261
00:15:25,758 --> 00:15:27,092
It's Torihara.

262
00:15:29,845 --> 00:15:32,264
I was worried, so I rushed here by car.

263
00:15:32,348 --> 00:15:35,726
I thought you might be shocked
after watching the broadcast.

264
00:15:38,729 --> 00:15:39,980
Mr. Konta,

265
00:15:40,064 --> 00:15:44,109
I think this episode
turned out quite well.

266
00:15:45,486 --> 00:15:46,654
What?

267
00:15:47,613 --> 00:15:50,366
I believe your charm
and essence as a person

268
00:15:50,449 --> 00:15:52,576
were properly conveyed to the viewers.

269
00:15:55,955 --> 00:15:57,706
Are you talking about that footage?

270
00:16:01,251 --> 00:16:05,047
I was shown like an idiot,
made a laughingstock online.

271
00:16:05,965 --> 00:16:08,634
It isn't even about me
being an actor anymore!

272
00:16:10,010 --> 00:16:11,720
Everyone looks down on me.

273
00:16:13,222 --> 00:16:14,473
I'm finished.

274
00:16:16,350 --> 00:16:18,185
My acting career is over.

275
00:16:19,937 --> 00:16:21,021
Mr. Konta,

276
00:16:21,105 --> 00:16:24,858
I thought that was exactly
what makes you charming.

277
00:16:25,609 --> 00:16:26,819
What?

278
00:16:26,902 --> 00:16:28,779
Everyone wants to see flawed people.

279
00:16:28,862 --> 00:16:30,823
People grow attached to flawed people.

280
00:16:30,906 --> 00:16:33,409
That's your unique charm
that no other actor has!

281
00:16:33,492 --> 00:16:36,286
This episode conveyed that to the viewers.

282
00:16:37,955 --> 00:16:40,290
Mr. Konta, you get easily carried away,

283
00:16:40,374 --> 00:16:44,169
so if I had encouraged you more,
you would have shown us more antics.

284
00:16:44,253 --> 00:16:46,088
But I thought that would be wrong.

285
00:16:46,171 --> 00:16:49,425
Actually, the producer
told me to stir you up more.

286
00:16:52,094 --> 00:16:58,392
I believe your charm, Mr. Konta,
lies in how you do your best for others

287
00:16:58,475 --> 00:17:01,061
when no one is watching
and no one asked you to,

288
00:17:01,145 --> 00:17:04,231
and how purely you enjoy happiness.

289
00:17:04,314 --> 00:17:05,941
That's what I intended to film.

290
00:17:07,901 --> 00:17:11,321
Mr. Konta, you're the best
just the way you are.

291
00:17:12,031 --> 00:17:13,490
I came here to say that.

292
00:17:14,033 --> 00:17:15,409
Now, excuse me.

293
00:17:32,009 --> 00:17:33,177
Hello?

294
00:17:41,602 --> 00:17:43,604
What? What's wrong?

295
00:17:43,687 --> 00:17:44,897
It's decided!

296
00:17:44,980 --> 00:17:46,231
What is?

297
00:17:47,066 --> 00:17:48,817
-A movie!
-What?

298
00:17:48,901 --> 00:17:52,529
Apparently, a movie director who watched
the documentary is making a film

299
00:17:52,613 --> 00:17:54,239
on the Tenpo famine for his next work,

300
00:17:54,323 --> 00:17:56,742
and they want to film
a peasant eating grass,

301
00:17:56,825 --> 00:17:58,410
and he wants to cast me for it!

302
00:17:58,494 --> 00:17:59,411
Hey!

303
00:17:59,495 --> 00:18:01,413
-You did it, Konta!
-I did it!

304
00:18:01,497 --> 00:18:02,998
The Great Tenpo famine…

305
00:18:03,082 --> 00:18:04,208
A historical piece?

306
00:18:04,291 --> 00:18:07,795
-A period movie!
-Just getting a role is wonderful!

307
00:18:07,878 --> 00:18:08,796
I'm happy!

308
00:18:08,879 --> 00:18:11,173
-You're an actor!
-Congratulations!

309
00:18:11,256 --> 00:18:12,299
Congratulations!

310
00:18:12,382 --> 00:18:13,342
Yay!

311
00:18:13,425 --> 00:18:15,719
Konta! Congratulations!

312
00:18:17,054 --> 00:18:18,305
Congratulations!

313
00:18:18,388 --> 00:18:19,431
Wow!

314
00:18:19,515 --> 00:18:21,725
-You did it!
-Thanks, Rinrin.

315
00:18:21,809 --> 00:18:24,645
Congratulations! You really did it!

316
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:48,127
Who might you be?

317
00:18:48,210 --> 00:18:49,711
Focus!

318
00:18:51,296 --> 00:18:52,631
<i>Obon </i>holidays, huh.

319
00:18:52,714 --> 00:18:54,550
What do we do on <i>Obon</i>, again?

320
00:18:54,633 --> 00:18:58,846
<i>Shouldn't we at least visit Midori's</i>
<i>grandma's grave? She built this villa.</i>

321
00:18:58,929 --> 00:19:01,473
-Grandma's photos!
-Wow!

322
00:19:02,474 --> 00:19:03,767
Ta-da!

323
00:19:03,851 --> 00:19:05,561
Oh, so cute!

324
00:19:05,644 --> 00:19:08,063
-Yay!
-So cute.

325
00:19:08,147 --> 00:19:10,732
Hey, the two of them left together!

326
00:19:11,567 --> 00:19:14,862
<i>This way</i>
<i>Grandma can return to the villa too.</i>

327
00:19:15,737 --> 00:19:18,448
<i>I'm home, Mr. Nishigami.</i>

328
00:19:18,949 --> 00:19:20,993
<i>Did you get a girlfriend?</i>

329
00:19:22,077 --> 00:19:26,790
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.
